 "transcript": {
  "answer": "**Victoria's unemployment rate is higher.** In September 2026 (seasonally adjusted), Victoria was at **5.1%** and NSW at **4.7%**, a gap of **0.3 percentage points** (0.35 points before rounding).\n\nThe gap has narrowed a little since mid-year. In June, Victoria was at 5.1% and NSW at 4.0%, a gap of about 1.1 points. NSW rose sharply in September, from 4.4% in August to 4.7%, while Victoria eased slightly from 5.2% to 5.1%.",
